                    title: "Gold star: the music staff",
                    explain: "Sheet music uses five lines called a staff. Notes sit on lines or in spaces. The lines, bottom to top, spell E G B D F: Every Good Boy Does Fine. The spaces spell F A C E. Higher on the staff means a higher note.",
                    facts: [
                        "A whole note lasts 4 beats, a half note 2, a quarter note 1.",
                        "This part is optional. Tab works great too!",
                    ],
                    visual: Some(Durations),
